Note: the /{code} pattern also matches /anything-without-a-slash. For example, /favicon.ico? No тАФ /favicon.ico has a dot, but the pattern `/{code}` matches any single segment, including "favicon.ico". So GET /favicon.ico тЖТ 404 link not found. That's fine, it's standard behavior for this design.

Important: in Go 1.22+ mux, literal patterns take precedence over wildcards, and multi-segment patterns like /api/links/{code}/stats take precedence over /{code} when the path has multiple segments. A 7-character code contains no slash, so /{code} only matches single-segment paths. No conflict.

