Hmm, reading one byte at a time from crypto/rand is a bit slow, but fine for a short service. Actually better: read in a loop until we have codeLength valid bytes:

```go
func randomCode() (string, error) {
	code := make([]byte, codeLength)
	n := 0
	for n < codeLength {
		var buf [16]byte
		k, err := rand.Read(buf[:])
		if err != nil {
			return "", err
		}
		for i := range k {
			if n >= codeLength {
				break
			}
			if buf[i] >= 248 {
				continue
			}
			code[n] = base62Alphabet[buf[i]%62]
			n++
		}
	}
	return string(code), nil
}
```

This is better. 248 = 4*62, so bytes 0..247 map uniformly to 0..61 via %62.

