Let me think about this: 16 bytes тЖТ each byte can yield at most 1 character? No wait. If I discard bytes тЙе 248 and use b%62, then 16 bytes yield at most 16 characters, but I need 7. Probability that 16 bytes all yield valid characters: (248/256)^16 тЙИ (0.96875)^16 тЙИ 0.602. So about 60% of the time one read is sufficient, otherwise loop. This matches "a single 16-byte read is almost always sufficient" (60% of the time).

